--- a/docs/search.md
+++ b/docs/search.md
@@ -181,6 +181,19 @@ screen's `draft.rs` retains a draft across successive input events while the fra
 frozen. A prediction publishes the completed replacement once, without exposing an intermediate
 deleted word to the store.
 
+OTT scalar editors declare a required `OttEditor.text_policy`: `Predictive` for
+human-readable names and search queries, or `Literal` for machine strings such as
+URLs, paths, credentials, identifiers and numeric settings. The field's producer
+chooses this typed policy; the screen does not guess from its key, contents or
+password masking. Literal commits insert the complete committed fragment at the
+caret through the existing buffer. Other editing operations and limits are unchanged.
+Ordinary Search keeps its whole-word prediction behavior.
+
+The normalized protocol has committed text and character-wise caret operations,
+not a preedit lifecycle or selection range. Literal entry does not add either API
+or infer missing composition events. Save/Cancel, addressed acknowledgements,
+validation and secret redaction remain the existing editor and owner contracts.
+
 The normalized input vocabulary carries a whole immutable `TextEdit::Commit`, plus Backspace,
 Clear, Left and Right. Keyboard ownership edges take effect in delivery order, including several
 edges in one frame; the page keeps its focus read while `Cx.owner` is `System(Keyboard)`.
